      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glencoe%2C_Minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Settlers erected a log schoolhouse in 1856, just a year after Glencoe was founded, to welcome eager children.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://historyofglencoe.blogspot.com/p/glencoe-mn.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town was planned by the railroad, and a nearby gas boom later attracted factories to Glencoe.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://hometownhistorymaps.com/pages/history-of-glencoe-minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Glencoe serves as the county seat of McLeod County, making it the administrative hub for the region.",
